<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate.ejs") %>
<main class="container py-4">
  <p style="color: #fe424d">This is a sample privacy page!</p>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>
    Thank you for using our travel website. This Privacy Policy explains what
    personal data we collect, why we collect it, how we use it, and your rights.
    Replace <strong>Travel Mate</strong> and contact details before publishing.
  </p>

  <h3>What we collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account and booking information</strong> — name; email; phone;
      billing address; passport or ID when required.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payment information</strong> — processed by third-party payment
      providers; we only receive transaction confirmations and masked
      identifiers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Travel preferences and itineraries</strong> — trip dates;
      destinations; accommodations; special requests.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Communications</strong> — support messages, feedback, and
      correspondence.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Device and usage data</strong> — IP address; browser; pages
      visited; cookies and similar technologies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Location data</strong> — when you permit it for features like
      local recommendations.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How we use your data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      To provide and manage bookings, confirmations, changes, and customer
      support.
    </li>
    <li>To process payments via secure third-party processors.</li>
    <li>
      To send transactional messages such as receipts, reminders, and travel
      alerts.
    </li>
    <li>
      To send marketing messages only if you opt in; you may opt out anytime.
    </li>
    <li>
      To improve services through analytics, personalization, and fraud
      detection.
    </li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and enforce our Terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Sharing and disclosure</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> — payment processors, email, analytics,
      hosting.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Travel partners</strong> — hotels, airlines, tour operators when
      needed to complete bookings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal and safety</strong> — when required by law or to protect
      rights or safety.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business transfers</strong> — in connection with mergers or asset
      sales.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Data retention and security</h3>
  <p>
    We retain data as needed to provide services and meet legal requirements. We
    implement reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect data,
    including encryption where possible. No online system is perfectly secure.
  </p>

  <h3>Your rights</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Access, correction, deletion, restriction, or portability where
      applicable.
    </li>
    <li>
      To exercise rights contact
      <strong>aravatanish866@gmail.com</strong>. We may require verification
      before fulfilling requests.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cookies and tracking</h3>
  <p>
    We use cookies for functionality, analytics, and advertising. You can
    control cookie settings in your browser and use industry opt-outs for
    targeted advertising.
  </p>

  <h3>Children</h3>
  <p>
    Services are not intended for children under 16. We do not knowingly collect
    data from children under 16.
  </p>

  <h3>International transfers</h3>
  <p>
    Data may be transferred and stored outside your jurisdiction. We use
    safeguards such as standard contractual clauses or reputable providers with
    adequate protections.
  </p>

  <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
  <p>
    We update this policy when necessary and publish the updated date on this
    page.
  </p>

  <h3>Contact</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Company</strong>: Travel Mate<br />
    <strong>Email</strong>: aravatanish866@gmail.com<br />
    <strong>Address</strong>: xyz
  </p>
